tags: statement-retention, retention_days

A promise of the node: how long it keeps the movements of a dead account, in days,
after the last movement of the account.

The value is days, in base 10. Example: 30. The value 0 means for ever. The node never
deletes the movements of an account that lives, or of a dead account with an account
alive below it.

With no promise, the caller assumes nothing. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
name=statement-retention
rule=the node keeps the movements of a dead account for at least value days after its last movement
value=days, base 10; 0 is for ever
